    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0174" n="166" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg166"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1447: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant to the Representative of the
                        President</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ocheltree</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-07-13T11:00:00-06:00">July 13, 1939—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Referring to Department’s telegram No. 34, July 11, 7 p.m., Licenciado Zúñiga
                    Montúfar has consented to my visiting Tegucigalpa in connection with the
                    mediation and has agreed to setting October 1st as a tentative date for an
                    executive session of the Commission.</p>
                <p>I am proceeding to Tegucigalpa by plane tomorrow.</p>
                <p>With reference to the Department’s telegram No. 35,<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d233-f1"/> please inform me at Tegucigalpa whether airplane travel
                    to Washington is authorized.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ocheltree</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d233-f1" n="37" xml:id="d233-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 35, July 12, 7 p.m., contained travel orders (715.1715/1445b
                    suppl.).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
